{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://docs.oasis-open.org/sarif/sarif/v2.1.0/errata01/os/schemas/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "grype",
          "version": "0.121.0",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-92392-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-92392 high vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "During an upload, curl mishandles HTTP/2 `RST_STREAM` received from the server (with reason `HTTP_1_1_REQUIRED` or `REFUSED_STREAM`) leading to a use after free of a `struct Curl_easy` object."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-92392",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-92392\nSeverity: high\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.22.0-1\nFix Version: 8.23.0-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-92392](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-92392)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-92392**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | curl  | 8.22.0-1  | 8.23.0-1  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-92392](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-92392)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/curl@8.22.0-1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-92392-libcurl4t64",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-92392 high vulnerability for libcurl4t64 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "During an upload, curl mishandles HTTP/2 `RST_STREAM` received from the server (with reason `HTTP_1_1_REQUIRED` or `REFUSED_STREAM`) leading to a use after free of a `struct Curl_easy` object."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-92392",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-92392\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libcurl4t64\nVersion: 8.22.0-1\nFix Version: 8.23.0-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-92392](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-92392)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-92392**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | libcurl4t64  | 8.22.0-1  | 8.23.0-1  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-92392](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-92392)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libcurl4t64@8.22.0-1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=curl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-82560-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-82560 high vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Pod::Text versions before 6.1.1 for Perl allow CPU and memory exhaustion formatting a POD document whose =over nesting drives the margin to the output width.  Each =over adds its indent to the margin, which wrap() subtracts from the output width to get the space available for text. When that space reaches zero, the line-splitting substitution matches the empty string, and the loop consumes no input while appending the margin padding on every pass.  Formatting an attacker-supplied POD document never returns, and the output grows until memory is exhausted."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-82560",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-82560\nSeverity: high\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.42.3-1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-82560](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-82560)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-82560**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | perl-base  | 5.42.3-1  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-82560](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-82560)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/perl-base@5.42.3-1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2017-17740-libldap2",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2017-17740 low vulnerability for libldap2 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "contrib/slapd-modules/nops/nops.c in OpenLDAP through 2.4.45, when both the nops module and the memberof overlay are enabled, attempts to free a buffer that was allocated on the stack, which allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (slapd crash) via a member MODDN operation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2017-17740",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2017-17740\nSeverity: low\nPackage: libldap2\nVersion: 2.6.14+dfsg-2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2017-17740](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2017-17740)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2017-17740**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | libldap2  | 2.6.14+dfsg-2  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2017-17740](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2017-17740)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libldap2@2.6.14%2Bdfsg-2?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=openldap"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-107708-libgssapi-krb5-2",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-107708 medium vulnerability for libgssapi-krb5-2 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "MIT krb5 through 1.22.2 contains a NULL pointer dereference vulnerability in the KDC's get_pac_princ_with_realm() that returns success while leaving the client principal NULL on malformed names. A malicious or compromised cross-realm trusted KDC can send an S4U2Proxy request with a PAC carrying a malformed client name to crash krb5kdc and deny authentication."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-107708",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-107708\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libgssapi-krb5-2\nVersion: 1.22.1-3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-107708](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-107708)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-107708**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libgssapi-krb5-2  | 1.22.1-3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-107708](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-107708)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libgssapi-krb5-2@1.22.1-3?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=krb5"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.9"
              }
