            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-107778-libgssapi-krb5-2",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-107778 high vulnerability for libgssapi-krb5-2 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "MIT Kerberos 5 (krb5) through 1.22.2 contains a NULL pointer dereference in make_cred_list() in rd_cred.c that allows authenticated Kerberos clients to crash services by sending mismatched KRB-CRED arrays. Attackers can send forwarded credentials with more tickets than ticket_info entries through gss_accept_sec_context() to crash GSS-API acceptor services, causing denial of service."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-107778",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-107778\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libgssapi-krb5-2\nVersion: 1.22.1-3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-107778](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-107778)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-107778**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | libgssapi-krb5-2  | 1.22.1-3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-107778](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-107778)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libgssapi-krb5-2@1.22.1-3?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=krb5"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-107778-libk5crypto3",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-107778 high vulnerability for libk5crypto3 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "MIT Kerberos 5 (krb5) through 1.22.2 contains a NULL pointer dereference in make_cred_list() in rd_cred.c that allows authenticated Kerberos clients to crash services by sending mismatched KRB-CRED arrays. Attackers can send forwarded credentials with more tickets than ticket_info entries through gss_accept_sec_context() to crash GSS-API acceptor services, causing denial of service."
