            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-107929-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-107929 low vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When `CURLOPT_INTERFACE` (or the command line tool's `--interface` option) is set with one of the documented prefixes (`if!`, `host!`, `ifhost!`), that binding is not part of the connection reuse key, so a later transfer asking for a different source can silently reuse an existing connection and go out from the earlier transfer's source address"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-107929",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-107929\nSeverity: low\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.22.0-1\nFix Version: 8.23.0-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-107929](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-107929)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-107929**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | curl  | 8.22.0-1  | 8.23.0-1  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-107929](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-107929)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/curl@8.22.0-1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian"
                ],
                "security-severity": "0.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-87861-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-87861 low vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When using ambient user credentials, an HTTP request directed to one origin may be dispatched over a connection previously authenticated via Negotiate for a different origin, leaving the request's intended credentials unused."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-87861",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-87861\nSeverity: low\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.22.0-1\nFix Version: 8.23.0~rc1-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-87861](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-87861)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-87861**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | curl  | 8.22.0-1  | 8.23.0~rc1-1  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-87861](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-87861)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/curl@8.22.0-1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian"
                ],
                "security-severity": "0.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-87862-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-87862 low vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Importing a `includeSubDomains` parent HSTS entry before a longer-lived child entry, silently drops the child. Consequently, when the parent expires, the child's valid HSTS policy is lost, causing curl to issue unencrypted HTTP requests rather than upgrading to HTTPS."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-87862",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-87862\nSeverity: low\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.22.0-1\nFix Version: 8.23.0~rc1-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-87862](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-87862)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-87862**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | curl  | 8.22.0-1  | 8.23.0~rc1-1  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-87862](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-87862)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/curl@8.22.0-1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian"
                ],
                "security-severity": "0.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-87863-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-87863 low vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An authenticated HTTPS origin can supply an HSTS `max-age` value that the parser accepts, but time serialization later fails to process. On 64-bit systems, extreme max-age values compute an absolute expiry within standard time integer limits that exceeds calendar time structure bounds. During cache saves, the original HSTS file is truncated before writing a temporary replacement; when serialization fails, the temporary file is deleted, leaving an empty or partial cache. Because the save error is silently ignored during cleanup, curl exits successfully despite the data loss."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-87863",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-87863\nSeverity: low\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.22.0-1\nFix Version: 8.23.0~rc1-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-87863](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-87863)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-87863**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | curl  | 8.22.0-1  | 8.23.0~rc1-1  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-87863](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-87863)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/curl@8.22.0-1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian"
                ],
                "security-severity": "0.0"
              }
            },
