            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-87863-libcurl4t64",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-87863 low vulnerability for libcurl4t64 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An authenticated HTTPS origin can supply an HSTS `max-age` value that the parser accepts, but time serialization later fails to process. On 64-bit systems, extreme max-age values compute an absolute expiry within standard time integer limits that exceeds calendar time structure bounds. During cache saves, the original HSTS file is truncated before writing a temporary replacement; when serialization fails, the temporary file is deleted, leaving an empty or partial cache. Because the save error is silently ignored during cleanup, curl exits successfully despite the data loss."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-87863",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-87863\nSeverity: low\nPackage: libcurl4t64\nVersion: 8.22.0-1\nFix Version: 8.23.0~rc1-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-87863](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-87863)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-87863**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | libcurl4t64  | 8.22.0-1  | 8.23.0~rc1-1  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-87863](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-87863)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libcurl4t64@8.22.0-1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=curl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "0.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-86412-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-86412 low vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A remote HTTP server can set a cookie that curl accepts and writes to a Netscape cookie jar but cannot reload. On the next invocation using the same path for `--cookie` and `--cookie-jar`, curl fails before connecting, then the cleanup procedure replaces the jar with an empty file, deleting cookies for unrelated domains."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-86412",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-86412\nSeverity: low\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.22.0-1\nFix Version: 8.23.0~rc1-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-86412](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-86412)",
