              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/curl@8.22.0-1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian"
                ],
                "security-severity": "0.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-86414-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-86414 low vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An HTTP proxy can trick libcurl into sending the origin's credentials (Basic password, or a Negotiate/Kerberos ticket) to the proxy itself, by answering the `CONNECT` tunnel request with 401 `WWW-Authenticate:` instead of the expected 407 `Proxy-Authenticate:`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-86414",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-86414\nSeverity: low\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.22.0-1\nFix Version: 8.23.0~rc1-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-86414](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-86414)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-86414**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | curl  | 8.22.0-1  | 8.23.0~rc1-1  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-86414](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-86414)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/curl@8.22.0-1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian"
                ],
                "security-severity": "0.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-92388-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-92388 low vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When an FTP wildcard `LIST` operation fails, libcurl omits the restoration path meant for successful listings, leaving the write callback set to the internal listing parser and the write callback data pointing directly to the easy handle. Subsequent reuse of this handle triggers an immediate crash, and cloning it via `curl_easy_duphandle()` copies this corrupted state into the duplicate. If the original handle is subsequently freed, executing a transfer on the cloned handle causes a heap use-after-free read against the dangling handle reference; alternatively, reusing the original or cloned handle while changing only  `CURLOPT_WRITEDATA` (and omitting `CURLOPT_WRITEFUNCTION`) results in type confusion, forcing the internal parser to interpret incoming server response bytes into memory at the application-supplied write data pointer."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-92388",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-92388\nSeverity: low\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.22.0-1\nFix Version: 8.23.0~rc1-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-92388](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-92388)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-92388**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | curl  | 8.22.0-1  | 8.23.0~rc1-1  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-92388](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-92388)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/curl@8.22.0-1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian"
                ],
                "security-severity": "0.0"
              }
            },
