            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-111497-libbrotli1",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-111497 low vulnerability for libbrotli1 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A buffer overflow vulnerability in the Brotli decoder (c/dec/decode.c) in Google Brotli versions 1.0.3 through 1.2.0 on all platforms allows a remote unauthenticated attacker to corrupt adjacent decoder state memory, disclose sensitive memory contents, cause a denial of service, or potentially execute arbitrary code using a crafted Brotli-compressed stream.\n\n\n\n\n\nUsers need to update any Brotli libraries or binaries between 1.0.3 through 1.2.0 to the latest available version: 1.0.10 or 1.1.1 or 1.2.1."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-111497",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-111497\nSeverity: low\nPackage: libbrotli1\nVersion: 1.2.0-4+b1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-111497](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-111497)",
